  "name": "Dirt",
  "tagline": "Loose gravel, no long straights — all transitions and two hairpins",
  "difficulty": "Loose",
  "notes": [
    "Retraced. The first version had six corners, none tighter than 173 m, and the slowest was a 117 km/h sweeper -- on gravel that is a circle you slide around, not a stage.",
    "No long straight, on purpose. On a loose surface the fun is in the transitions, so this is twelve corners, most of them 85 to 200 m, and the car is changing direction almost continuously.",
    "Two hairpins at 44 and 48 m to break it up. On 0.62 grip those are the corners you can genuinely throw it into.",
    "Traced from straights and arcs, closure solved by least squares.",
    "Elevation is invented: two gentle waves over the lap."
  ],
